-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  intr_size.pcpp - Intrinsic compliance: size

  size(T) (BNF.md sec 7) is the byte size of a type as an int64: a builtin,
  a pointer, a record, an array type, a C/C++ type. Text that is plainly a
  type is parsed as one; a lone name must name a type (a value is an error).
  It is a constant.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\intr_size.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\intr_size.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    int64 8
    ptr 8
    record 8
    array 16
    cpp 2
    constant 8
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    intr_size_err_value.pcpp
      size of a variable (SM0410)
    intr_size_err_args.pcpp
      size with no argument (SM0409)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe intr_size;

#include <cstdint>

type
  TPoint = record
    X: int32;
    Y: int32;
  end;

begin
  println("int64 {}", size(int64));
  println("ptr {}", size(ptr to char));
  println("record {}", size(TPoint));
  println("array {}", size(array[0..3] of int32));
  println("cpp {}", size(std::int16_t));
  println("constant {}", size(int32) * 2);
end.
